    "updated_at": "2023-02-01T13:36:25Z",
    "body": "Same here with `fish, version 3.6.0`. And it's pretty painful since I have quite a few custom modules. Is there a chance of introducing a native plugin system?\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1369559/216045144-e5422a9c-3f27-4fe3-99c8-29894744db1a.png)\r\n\r\nSetting `shell: [\"sh\", \"--norc\"]` is not a fit in many cases. F.i. in the following one:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[custom.custom_nix_shell]\r\nsymbol = \"x\"\r\nwhen = 'test -n \"$IN_NIX_SHELL\" || test -n \"$IN_NIX_RUN\"'\r\nstyle = \"bold blue dimmed\"\r\nformat = \"[\\\\[$symbol$state\\\\]]($style) \"\r\n```\r\n\r\n(when access to the actual shell's env is essential)\r\n\r\n--- \r\n\r\nFor now, to work around the issue, I made use of https://github.com/acomagu/fish-async-prompt setting it up to async-render only `fish_right_prompt`, where I moved all the expensive modules to.\r\n\r\n```fish\r\n# config.fish\r\nfunction fish_right_prompt_loading_indicator -a last_prompt\r\n    echo -n \"$last_prompt\" | string trim --chars ↻ --left | string trim --left | read -zl last_prompt_trimmed_loading\r\n    echo -n \"↻ $last_prompt_trimmed_loading\"\r\nend\r\n\r\nset async_prompt_functions fish_right_prompt\r\n```\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n# starship.toml\r\nformat = \"\"\"\r\n$directory\\\r\n$git_branch\\\r\n$git_commit\\\r\n$git_state\\\r\n$git_metrics\\\r\n$git_status\\\r\n$character\"\"\"\r\n\r\n# move the rest of the prompt to the right\r\nright_format = \"\"\"\r\n$cmd_duration\\\r\n${custom.custom_direnv}\\\r\n${custom.custom_nix_shell}\\\r\n$all\\\r\n$shell\\\r\n$shlvl\"\"\"\r\n```\r\nhere is the demo:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1369559/216057749-0bad7783-a7fd-43f9-9900-59022c4833f4.mp4\r\n",
